The discussion below contains minor spoiler information
about enchanting weapons, and an error in the WCST file.

SPOILER ALERT


I had previously written:

>If a weapon starts out at > +5 (i.e., is currently +6 or more) when 
>you read a blessed or uncursed enchant weapon scroll, there is a 2/3
>chance of it evaporating.

To which Andrew Trapp replied:

>According to my copy of the WCST spoilers file, the odds are (above +5)
>2/3 that you will _succeed_, not fail.

What Andrew says is true; the WCST file does say that.  However, the
applicable source code from "wield.c" reads:

   /* there is a (soft) upper and lower limit to uwep->spe */
   if(((uwep->spe > 5 && amount > 0) || (uwep->spe < -5 && amount < 0))
							&& rn2(3)) {

"rn2(3)" will return from 0 to 2.  If it returns 1 or 2, the "if"
conditional would be true and the "evaporate" code would be executed.
Therefore, the WCST file is in error!!!



